  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Monday...\n\nWindy conditions will continue today as the influence of an upper\nlow moving across southern Canada remains over the region. West to\nnorthwest winds gusting 20 to 45 mph will be common, with the \nstrongest gusts in eastern Montana. The chance for precipitation\ntoday will be fairly low, with the exception of isolated showers\nand thunderstorms late this afternoon and evening as a weak wave\nmoves across the state. The primary concerns with any activity\nwill be gusty winds.\n\nWhile temperatures will be slightly below normal today (highs in \nthe 70s to around 80), the dry and windy conditions will result \nin elevated fire weather conditions.\n\nWarmer and drier conditions continue Wednesday and Thursday, with\ntemperatures climbing back into the 80s to low 90s (warmest\nThursday). Breezy winds will continue each day, with gusts in the\n20s to 40s mph, strongest in the foothills west of Billings and \nall area mountains each day. The combination of above normal\ntemperatures, low relative humidity values, and windy conditions\nwill bring elevated fire weather conditions each day, especially\nThursday. Please take care not to cause a spark!\n\nLooking towards Friday and the weekend, forecast certainty\ndecreases. Several modals continue to show a cooler and wetter\nsystem digging into the region but disagree on the track at this\ntime. Mountain snowfall will be possible with this system so\ncontinue to monitor the forecast if you have outdoor plans in the\nhigh country! Matos",
